    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking for some advice on pallet stacking for our new high-density racking system in the warehouse. we're dealing with some pretty heavy industrial loads and i'm worried about stability when we stack them high. specifically, what's the best way to handle the center of gravity and any interlocking patterns you'd recommend to keep things from shifting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To maintain stability for heavy, high-density loads, position pallets squarely and ensure their centers of gravity are vertically aligned directly above the base layer to prevent tipping. Use an interlocking stacking pattern, such as a bricklay method, to distribute weight evenly and restrict lateral movement between pallets. Always rely on your manufacturer's load charts and guide rails, as relying on estimation for high-height configurations is unsafe in industrial environments.",
